<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="e979a6f7">&lt;p&gt;
    Educate key client stakeholders on the risks that could arise from failures around security and controls and how EY&apos;s
    unique approach can help mitigate these risks. Conduct workshops that focus on specific topics such as the following:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;strong&gt;Risk and internal controls&lt;/strong&gt;including business process controls, IT general controls, application
        configuration controls, controls orchestration, etc.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;strong&gt;Application and data security&lt;/strong&gt;including application roles, segregation of duties (SOD), sensitive
        access (SA), authentication, etc.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;strong&gt;User identity and governance&lt;/strong&gt; including user access management, user and role certification,
        enterprise and application role governance, etc.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;strong&gt;Evolving risk management&lt;/strong&gt; including application change and release management, license management,
        internal controls management, etc.
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="externalId" nodeId="5f7555cc"></attribute>
<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="a3eb9155">Oracle trusted workshops are typically conducted very early on, at times even before the statement of work (SOW) is signed,
in order to allow the client to make key decisions around security and controls.</attribute>
